Ticket [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds <ProblemCount ticket={4471} total /> reports. They are
not one bug. Read report by report, they are three problems, and each needs its own fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is three problems, not one. The queued parser fix covers only the first.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

1. **The shared parser reads dates month first:** <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports.
   Our tenants write the day first, so 7 April comes out as 4 July. Day and month swap.
   This is the desk's own count: it includes the <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="hiddenInParser" /> one-day moves,
   counted where the desk files them.
   [Issue #1](https://github.com/Nairelav/megadev-formation/issues/1).
2. **The booking-v3 form hint says MM/DD/YYYY:** <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports.
   People at booking-v3 tenants type the month first because the hint tells them to, and the form
   reads it the tenant's way. The swap looks the same, but the fix is the form hint, not the parser.
   [Issue #2](https://github.com/Nairelav/megadev-formation/issues/2).
3. **Dates move by one day:** <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="one-day" /> reports.
   Nothing swaps. The date lands one day early or late. One report has the same meeting on Tuesday
   in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. This looks like a time zone bug, and the parser fix will not touch it.
   [Issue #3](https://github.com/Nairelav/megadev-formation/issues/3).

The ticket export has <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="rows" /> rows. <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="duplicateRows" />
of them repeat a report, so they are counted once.

## What the #4471 page gets wrong

- Its cause table counts the <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="hiddenInParser" /> one-day moves inside
  the parser row and only footnotes them, so they never show up as a problem of their own.
- It marks the hint row "not this ticket — no ticket of its own", so that bug has no ticket at all.
- Its "tagged as" column shows intake's guess, made from the reporter's browser. For
  <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="intakeWrong" /> reports that guess disagrees with the cause the desk's own logic gives.
- Its timeline shows a spike that is not a surge. Nothing was merged for
  <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="weeksBeforeFirstMerge" /> weeks, then <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="bulkCount" />
  reports were merged in one go on <ProblemCount ticket={4471} fact="bulkDay" />. Reports came in at a steady rate the whole time.

## How the problems were told apart

Every count on this page is computed from `reports-4471.json` by `#lib/kb/problems.ts`, which reuses
the desk's own `causes.ts` and `locales.ts`. It uses the desk's own view of the export: `causes.ts` puts each report in
"parser" or "hint" by tenant, and the one-day moves are the desk's footnote over `desk-notes.json`.
The one-day moves stay counted under "parser" as well, so the three counts add up to more than the
number of reports.

